    "result_text": "All 29 tests pass. The change is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the city-capacity rule: creating an owner is now rejected with **409 Conflict** when the owner's city already contains 50 or more owners.\n\nChanges, following the existing owner-rule patterns in the codebase:\n\n1. **`CityAtCapacityException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` carrying the offending city, mirroring `DuplicateOwnerHouseholdException`/`DuplicateOwnerTelephoneException`.\n\n2. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` that maps `CityAtCapacityException` to `409 Conflict` with `errors: [\"city\"]`, consistent with the other duplicate handlers.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added a `CITY_CAPACITY = 50` constant and a `requireCityHasCapacity(...)` check invoked in `addOwner`, after the household check and before persistence. Cities are compared case-insensitively with collapsed whitespace via the existing `normalizeHousehold` helper, matching how the other household fields are compared.\n\nThe new `Cp18Tests` acceptance test passes (fill a city to 50, 51st is rejected with 409), and all 29 existing tests remain green.",
